ks it landed, and the epic\n201-becomes `versé` when a session finds that its stories deliver its purpose. The run starts from `main`\n202-with a clean tree and stops at the first block, saying why; it never pushes.\n203-`npm run cycle -- <story> auto` does the same for a single story.\n204-\n205-Three of the owner's answers are delegated, each an act recorded in the record:\naa79df16 docs: the registry no longer lists a gap of the change-lifecycle campaign left unarchived, which the campaign now keeps under test-output/formal-traces/reduced/\n30e5e3a2 test: a campaign failure that names no reduced-case file fails the property tests with its own error as cause instead of a bare absent file\ncf5afa61 refactor: the change-lifecycle campaign keeps reducedCase to itself, which only its own failure path reads\n719fd1b1 feat: the change-lifecycle campaign keeps the reduced case of a gap it finds on the kernel in a file of test-output/formal-traces/reduced/ named by its seed and path, then fails naming that file, and the injected-defect test reads its case from there\n286ee763 test: a gap the change-lifecycle campaign finds on the kernel leaves its reduced case in a file under test-output/formal-traces/reduced/, named by its seed and path, that its failure message names and that replays the same minimal sequence and failure\n690a5fab docs: the story e38s04 promises that a gap the change-lifecycle campaign finds on the kernel leaves its reduced case in a file under test-output/formal-traces/reduced/ that its failure message names and that replays the same minimal sequence\na9f862b2 docs: the registry records that a gap the change-lifecycle campaign finds on the real kernel is reported in the test failure but not archived as a reduced case\n06308fac test: a gap the 3000-sequence campaign finds on the kernel fails with the reduced case to keep, its seed, reduction path, versions and minimal sequence\nb12a2f4a test: a defect found by the property campaign is kept with a path t